# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# ROM-FIX FIX-001 migration: relabel NFC storage that a stock ROM left as
# system_data_file.
# file_contexts maps /data/nfc to nfc_data_file, but init's mkdir does not
# relabel a directory that already exists, so a dirty flash from stock keeps the
# old label and NFA storage fails with EACCES.
# --force: without it libselinux skips the tree when the directory's
# security.sehash matches the current file_contexts, which leaves a stale label in
# place after a chcon or a restored backup. /data/nfc holds a few files, so the
# cost is negligible.
on post-fs-data
    restorecon_recursive --force /data/nfc
